Project Name: Mercury Processing Platform
Final use case
    A production-style order processing platform for receiving customer orders, processing them asynchronously, storing order state durably, generating artifacts, and exposing operational visibility for reliability and recovery.

Functional flow
    Client sends order request to public endpoint
    Request reaches AWS ALB
    ALB forwards to API service in EKS
    API validates request
    API writes initial order record to PostgreSQL
    API publishes processing task to SQS
    Worker service consumes SQS message
    Worker processes order
    Worker updates PostgreSQL order status
    Worker stores generated artifact/report in S3
    Notification service logs or simulates downstream notification
    Prometheus/Grafana/Loki collect metrics and logs
    Failures route to retry/DLQ path


