 What each component does

You need to understand every box. If you cannot explain it, you do not own it.

ALB

    Public entry point. Routes HTTP/HTTPS traffic to Kubernetes ingress.

EKS

    Runs containerized workloads and platform services.

API service

    Accepts orders, validates them, writes initial state, pushes async work.

Worker service

    Consumes SQS messages, performs processing, updates DB, writes artifact to S3.

Notification service

    Simulates downstream system notification. Can begin as simple logger or webhook mock.

PostgreSQL

    Durable relational source of truth for orders and status transitions.

SQS + DLQ

    Buffers asynchronous jobs and isolates poison messages through dead-letter handling.

Redis

    Stores short-lived fast-access data like idempotency tokens or cached lookups.

S3

    Stores generated reports or artifacts.

Prometheus/Grafana/Loki

    Metrics, dashboards, logs, and troubleshooting.

GitHub Actions

    Automates build, push, deploy, and later infra workflows.


